    "result_text": "Tests pass. The change is complete.\n\nI extended the business-day rule in `BusinessDay.java` to cover public holidays:\n\n- Added the fixed public-holiday list (2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28) as a `Set<LocalDate>`.\n- Replaced the weekend-only switch with `adjust(...)` that rolls forward one day at a time until it lands on a business day, where a new `isBusinessDay(...)` helper treats a date as a business day only if it's a weekday *and* not a listed holiday.\n\nThis keeps the single-responsibility shape: `BusinessDay` remains the one place that defines a business day, so both `ResolveOwnerRegistrationDate` and the daily create-limit bucketing (`EnsureDailyOwnerLimit`) inherit the holiday rule for free \u2014 no logic duplicated. The loop also naturally handles a holiday adjacent to a weekend (e.g. 2026-12-25/28 near a weekend) by continuing to roll forward.\n\n`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
